\# Changelog



All notable changes to the AI Tag Language (ATL) specification will be documented in this file.



\## - 2026-03-16

\### Added

\- Launching the initial release of AI Tag Language (ATL) Specification.

\- Created `ATL\_v01.md` as the core system instruction file for direct AI injection.

\- Defined the 4 core architectural tag types for ATL:

&#x20; - \*\*Flag Tags\*\*: Binary trigger actions (e.g., `\[list]`, `\[result]`).

&#x20; - \*\*Type Tags\*\*: Output format specifiers (e.g., `\[file:pdf]`, `\[image:png]`).

&#x20; - \*\*Param Tags\*\*: Key-value configurations (e.g., `\[search:link]`, `\[size:100]`).

&#x20; - \*\*Special Tags\*\*: Non-executing engine rules (e.g., `//\[tag]//` for comments).

\## - 2026-03-16

\### Deleted

\- Removed [search] and [think] as it is unnecessary.

\- Removed [important] as it serves no useful purpose.



